          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            A
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"} topological space
            is called
            %em locally compact
            if every point has a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+topological+space"} compact
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/neighbourhood"} neighbourhood
          %p
            Or rather, if one does not at the same time assume that the space is
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hausdorff+topological+space"} Hausdorff topological space
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#LocalCompactnessViaCompactNeighbourhoodBase"}
            below) and possibily such that they are topological closures of smaller open neighbourhoods (def.
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#LocallyCompactSpace"}
            below).
          %p
            There are various definitions in use, which all coincide if the space is also
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hausdorff+topological+space"} Hausdorff
            (prop.
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#InHausdorffSpacesDefinitionsOfLocalCompactnessAgree"}
            below).
          %p
            Local compactness is one of the conditions that are often required by default for working with topological spaces: locally compact spaces are a class of “
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/nice+topological+spaces"}> nice topological spaces
            ”.
          %h2#definition Definition
          #LocalCompactnessViaCompactNeighbourhoodBase.num_defn
            %h6#definition_2 Definition
            %p
              %strong (local compactness via compact neighbourhood base)
            %p
              A
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"} topological space
              is
              %em locally compact
              if every point has a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/neighborhood+base"} neighborhood base
              consisting of
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+subspaces"} compact subspaces
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \in X
              every
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/open+neighbourhood"} open neighbourhood
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi x
                    %mo ⊃
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U_x \supset \{x\}
              contains a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+topological+space"} compact
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/neighbourhood"} neighbourhood
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi K
                        %mi x
                      %mo ⊂
                      %msub
                        %mi U
                        %mi x
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K_x \subset U_x
          %p Alternatively:
          #LocallyCompactSpace.num_defn
            %h6#definition_3 Definition
            %p
              %strong (local compactness via compact closures inside neighbourhoods)
            %p
              A
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"} topological space
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              is called
              %em locally compact
              if for every point
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \in X
              and every
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/open+neighbourhood"} open neighbourhood
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi x
                    %mo ⊃
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U_x \supset \{x\}
              there exists a smaller open neighbourhood
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi V
                      %mi x
                    %mo ⊂
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi x
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V_x \subset U_x
              whose
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+closure"} topological closure
              is
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+topological+space"} compact
              and still contained in
              = succeed ":" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi U
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %mo ⊂
                    %msub
                      %mi V
                      %mi x
                    %mo ⊂
                    %munder
                      %mrow
                        %mi Cl
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mi V
                          %mi x
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mtext compact
                    %mo ⊂
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi x
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\{x\} \subset V_x \subset \underset{\text{compact}}{Cl(V_x)} \subset U_x
                    \\,.
          #InHausdorffSpacesDefinitionsOfLocalCompactnessAgree.num_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p
              If
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hausdorff+topological+space"} Hausdorff topological space
              then definition
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#LocalCompactnessViaCompactNeighbourhoodBase"}
              is equivalent to definition
              = succeed "." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#LocallyCompactSpace"}
          .proof
            %h6#proof Proof
            %p
              Generally definition
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#LocallyCompactSpace"}
              implies definition
              = succeed "." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#LocalCompactnessViaCompactNeighbourhoodBase"}
            %p
              Hence assume that for every point
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \in X
              then every open neighbourhood
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi x
                    %mo ⊃
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U_x \supset \{x\}
              contains a compact neighbourhood. We need to show that it then also contains the closure
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Cl
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi V
                      %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Cl(V_x)
              of a smaller open neighbourhood and such that this closure is compact.
            %p
              So let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi K
                      %mi x
                    %mo ⊂
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi x
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K_x \subset U_x
              be a compact neighbourhood. Being a neighbourhood, it has a non-trivial
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/interior"} interior
              which is an open neighbourhood
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi Int
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi K
                      %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⊂
                    %msub
                      %mi K
                      %mi x
                    %mo ⊂
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi x
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi X
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\{x\} \subset Int(K_x) \subset K_x \subset U_x \subset X
                    \\,.
            %p
              Since
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+subspaces+of+Hausdorff+spaces+are+closed"} compact subspaces of Hausdorff spaces are closed
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi K
                      %mi x
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K_x \subset X
              is a closed subset. This implies that the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+closure"} topological closure
              of its interior as a subset of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              is still contained in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi K
                      %mi x
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K_x
              (since the topological closure is the smallest closed subset containing the given subset):
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Cl
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi Int
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi K
                        %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ⊂
                      %msub
                        %mi K
                        %mi x
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Cl(Int(K_x)) \subset K_x
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subsets+are+closed+in+a+closed+subspace+precisely+if+they+are+closed+in+the+ambient+space"} subsets are closed in a closed subspace precisely if they are closed in the ambient space
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Cl
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Int
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi K
                      %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Cl(Int(K_x))
              is also closed as a subset of the compact subspace
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi K
                        %mi x
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K_x
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/closed+subsets+of+compact+spaces+are+compact"} closed subsets of compact spaces are compact
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi K
                        %mi x
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K_x
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/continuous+images+of+compact+spaces+are+compact"} continuous images of compact spaces are compact
              = succeed ":" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi Int
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi K
                      %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⊂
                    %munder
                      %mrow
                        %mi Cl
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi Int
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mi K
                          %mi x
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mtext compact
                    %mo ⊂
                    %munder
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi K
                          %mi x
                      %mrow
                    %mo ⊂
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi x
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi X
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\{x\} \subset Int(K_x) \subset \underset{\text{compact}}{Cl(Int(K_x))} \subset \underset{}{K_x} \subset U_x \subset X
                    \\,.
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark Remark
            %p
              %strong (remark on terminology)
            %p
              As for
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+spaces"} compact spaces
              (
              %a{:href => "compact+space#DifferingTerminology"}> this remark
              ), some authors choose to include the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hausdorff+space"} Hausdorff
              condition as a matter of course, calling locally compact not-necessarily-Hausdorff spaces ‘locally quasi-compact’. We will not follow that convention here, but the reader should be warned that without the Hausdorff hypothesis, there are several inequivalent notions of local compactness in the literature; see
              %a{:href => "https://secure.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/wiki/Locally_compact_space"} the English Wikipedia
              for a survey and counterexamples.
            %p
              Note, however, that a topological space
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              satisfying Definition
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#LocallyCompactSpace"}
              is regular, because, as is immediate from the definition, closed neighbourhoods then form a neighbourhood basis of
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              be
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi T
                      %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T_{0}
              for it to in fact be Hausdorff.
          %h2#examples Examples
          .num_example
            %h6#example Example
            %p
              Every
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/discrete+space"} discrete space
              is locally compact.
          .num_example
            %h6#example_2 Example
            %p
              %strong
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/open+subspaces+of+compact+Hausdorff+spaces+are+locally+compact"}> open subspaces of compact Hausdorff spaces are locally compact
                )
            %p
              Every
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/open+subset"} open
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+subspace"} topological subspace
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %munder
                      %mo ⊂
                      %mtext open
                    %mi K
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \underset{\text{open}}{\subset} K
              of a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+topological+space"} compact
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hausdorff+space"} Hausdorff space
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi K
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
              is a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+compact+topological+space"} locally compact topological space
            %p
              In particular every
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+Hausdorff+space"} compact Hausdorff space
              itself is
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+compact+topological+space"} locally compact
            %p
              Conversely, every locally compact Hausdorff space
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              arises in this way, since it can be considered an open subspace in its
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/one-point+compactification"} one-point compactification
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                      %mo ⊔
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                      %mn ∞
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \sqcup \{\infty\}
              = succeed "." do
                %em
                  %a{:href => "one-point+compactification#LocallyCompatcHausdorffSpaceIsOpenSubspaceOfCompactHausdorffSpace"} this example
          #real.num_example
            %h6#example_3 Example
            %p
              The
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/real+numbers"} real numbers
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+numbers"} complex numbers
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝔭
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{p}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adic+completions"} adic completions
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebraic+number+fields"} algebraic number fields
              (with respect to a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/prime+ideal"} prime ideal
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝔭
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{p}
              in the
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ring+of+integers"} ring of integers
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/positive+characteristic"} positive characteristic
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi p
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Laurent+series"} Laurent series
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝔽
                      %mi q
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi t
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{F}_q((t))
              over a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+field"} finite field
              with
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi q
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} q
              elements, topologized with respect to a discrete valuation, is locally compact. In fact, any non-discrete locally compact
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field"} field
              must be of one of these types; they are called
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/local+fields"} local fields
          #product.num_example
            %h6#example_4 Example
            %p
              Finite
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/product+topological+spaces"} product topological spaces
              of locally compact spaces are locally compact.
          .num_example
            %h6#example_5 Example
            %p
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/closed+subspace"} Closed subspaces
              of locally compact spaces are locally compact. (Hence locally compact spaces form a
              = succeed ".)" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finitely+complete+category"} finitely complete category
          #TopologicalManifoldsAreLocallyCompact.num_example
            %h6#example_6 Example
            %p
              %strong
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+manifolds"} topological manifolds
                are
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+compact+topological+spaces"} locally compact topological spaces
            %p
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+manifolds"}> Topological manifolds
              , being locally
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homeomorphism"} homeomorphic
              to the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Euclidean+space"} Euclidean
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/metric+spaces"} metric spaces
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi ℝ
                        %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^n
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#real"}
              and
              = succeed "." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#product"}
            %p
              This applies also to
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+Euclidean+spaces"} locally Euclidean spaces
              which are not necessarily
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/paracompact+topological+space"} paracompact
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hausdorff+topological+spaces"} Hausdorff topological spaces
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/long+line"} long line
          %p
          #CountablyInfiniteProductsOfNonCompactSpacesAreNotLocallyCompact.num_remark
            %h6 Example
            %p
              %strong (countably infinite products of non-compact spaces are NOT locally compact)
              %br/
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              be a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"} topological space
              which is not
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+topological+space"} compact
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/product+topological+space"} product topological space
              of a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/countable+set"} countably infinite set
              of copies of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %munder
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∏
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi ℕ
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\underset{n \in \mathbb{N}}{\prod} X
            %p is not locally compact.
          .proof
            %h6#proof_2 Proof
            %p
              Since the
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/continuous+image+of+a+compact+space+is+compact"} continuous image of a compact space is compact
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/projection"} projection
              maps
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi p
                      %mi i
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %munder
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∏
                      %mi ℕ
                    %mi X
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p_i \;\colon\; \underset{\mathbb{N}}{\prod} X \longrightarrow X
              are continuous, it follows that every compact subspace of the product space is contained in one of the form
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %munder
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∏
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi ℕ
                    %msub
                      %mi K
                      %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\underset{i \in \mathbb{N}}{\prod} K_i
            %p
              for
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi K
                      %mi i
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K_i \subset X
              compact.
            %p
              But by the nature of the
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Tychonoff+topology"} Tychonoff topology
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/base+for+a+topology"} base for the topology
              on
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %munder
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∏
                      %mi ℕ
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \underset{\mathbb{N}}{\prod} X
              is given by subsets of the form
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mo (
                      %munder
                        %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∏
                        %mrow
                          %mi i
                          %mo ∈
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                          %mn 1
                          %mo ,
                          %mi ⋯
                          %mo ,
                          %mi n
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %msub
                        %mi U
                        %mi i
                      %mo )
                    %mo ×
                    %mrow
                      %mo (
                      %munder
                        %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∏
                        %mrow
                          %mi j
                          %mo ∈
                          %msub
                            %mi ℕ
                            %mrow
                              %mo &gt;
                              %mi n
                      %mi X
                      %mo )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\left(
                    \\underset{i \in \{1,\cdots,n\}}{\prod}
                    U_{i}
                    \\right)
                    \\times
                    \\left(
                    \\underset{j \in \mathbb{N}_{\gt n}}{\prod}
                    X
                    \\right)
            %p
              with
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi i
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U_i \subset X
              open. Hence every compact neighbourhood in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %munder
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∏
                      %mi ℕ
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \underset{\mathbb{N}}{\prod} X
              contains a subset of this kind, but if
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              itself is non-compact, then none of these is contained in a product of compact subsets.
          %p
          #RationalsAreNotLocallyCompact.num_remark
            %h6 Example
            %p
              %strong (non-example)
              The space of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rational+numbers"} rational numbers
              as a subspace of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/real+numbers"} real numbers
              with the Euclidean topology is not locally compact since its compact subsets all have empty interior.
          %h2#properties Properties
          %h3#general General
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition_2 Proposition
            %p
              %strong
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/proper+maps+to+locally+compact+spaces+are+closed"}> proper maps to locally compact spaces are closed
                )
            %p Let
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi X
                        %mo ,
                        %msub
                          %mi τ
                          %mi X
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (X,\tau_X)
                  be a
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"} topological space
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi Y
                        %mo ,
                        %msub
                          %mi τ
                          %mi Y
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (Y,\tau_Y)
                  a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+compact+topological+space"} locally compact topological space
                  according to def.
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#LocallyCompactSpace"}
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi f
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                        %mi X
                        %mo →
                        %mi Y
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f \colon X \to Y
                  a
                  = succeed "." do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/continuous+function"} continuous function
            %p Then:
            %p
              If
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
              is a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/proper+map"} proper map
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/closed+map"} closed map
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+compact+and+sigma-compact+spaces+are+paracompact"} locally compact and sigma-compact spaces are paracompact
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+compact+and+second-countable+spaces+are+sigma-compact"} locally compact and second-countable spaces are sigma-compact
          %h3#categorytheoretic_properties Category-theoretic properties
          %p
            Perhaps the most important consequence of local compactness (as defined above) for categorical topology is that locally compact spaces are
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/exponential+object"} exponentiable
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
            is locally compact, then
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Y
                  %mo ×
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo :
                  %mi Top
                  %mo →
                  %mi Top
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y \times -: Top \to Top
            has a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjunction"} right adjoint
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi Y
                    %mo :
                    %mi Top
                    %mo →
                    %mi Top
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (-)^Y: Top \to Top
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sober+spaces"} sober spaces
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locales"} locales
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+compact+locale"} locally compact
            if and only if it is exponentiable. (See
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/exponential+law+for+spaces"} exponential law for spaces
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact-open+topology"} compact-open topology
            for more details.)
          %p
            As noted above, locally compact spaces form a finitely complete
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/full+subcategory"} full subcategory
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Top
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Top
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi X
                    %mi p
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi K
                    %mi p
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mrow
                      %mi p
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi P
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (X_p, K_p)_{p \in P}
            be a collection of pairs of spaces where each
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi X
                    %mi p
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_p
            is locally compact and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi K
                    %mi p
                  %mo ⊆
                  %msub
                    %mi X
                    %mi p
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K_p \subseteq X_p
            is a compact
            %em open
            subspace. The
            %strong restricted direct product
            of the collection is the colimit of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/filtered+category"} filtered diagram
            consisting of spaces
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi D
                    %mi F
                  %mo =
                  %munder
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∏
                    %mrow
                      %mi p
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi F
                  %msub
                    %mi X
                    %mi p
                  %mo ×
                  %munder
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∏
                    %mrow
                      %mi p
                      %mo ∉
                      %mi F
                  %msub
                    %mi K
                    %mi p
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D_F = \prod_{p \in F} X_p \times \prod_{p \notin F} K_p
          %p
            where
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
            ranges over all finite subsets of
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi P
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi D
                    %mi F
                  %mo ⊆
                  %msub
                    %mi D
                    %mrow
                      %mi F
                      %mo ′
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D_F \subseteq D_{F'}
            where
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                    %mo ⊆
                    %mi F
                    %mo ′
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F \subseteq F'
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi D
                    %mi F
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D_F
            is locally compact, and that a filtered colimit or union of a system of
            %em open
            inclusions of locally compact spaces is again locally compact. Therefore, restricted direct products are locally compact, under the hypotheses stated above.
          %p
            These hypotheses are of course pretty severe; important examples of such restricted direct products include topologized
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adele+ring"} adele ring
            = succeed "s." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/idele+group"} idele group
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi K
                    %mi 𝔭
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi O
                    %mi 𝔭
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (K_{\mathfrak{p}}, O_{\mathfrak{p}})
            where
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi K
                    %mi 𝔭
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K_{\mathfrak{p}}
            is the
            = succeed "-adic" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝔭
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{p}
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/number+field"} number field
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi K
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi O
                    %mi 𝔭
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} O_{\mathfrak{p}}
            is the
            = succeed "-adic" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝔭
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{p}
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi O
                    %mo ⊆
                    %mi K
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} O \subseteq K
          %p
            In any event, the category of locally compact spaces does not admit general infinite products. If it did, then so would the category of locally compact Hausdorff spaces, and so would the category of locally compact Hausdorff abelian groups. However, there is no product of countably many copies of the real numbers in
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi LCHAb
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} LCHAb
          %p
            Locally compact spaces
            %em are
            closed under
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coproduct"} coproduct
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Top
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Top
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/colimit"} colimit
            %em raison d'être
            for
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compactly+generated+topological+spaces"} compactly generated topological spaces
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Top
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Top
            of diagrams of locally compact spaces (see also Prop.
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#HausdorffkSpacesAreQuotientsOfLCHausSpaces"}
            below).
          %h3#RelationToCompactlyGeneratedSpaces Relation to compactly generated spaces
          %p
          #LocallyCompactHausdorffSpacesAreCompactlyGeneratedWeaklyHausdorff.num_prop
            %h6 Proposition
            %p
              Every
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+compact+Hausdorff+space"} locally compact Hausdorff space
              is
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compactly+generated+topological+space"} compactly generated
              and
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weakly+Hausdorff+topological+space"} weakly Hausdorff
          (e.g.
          = succeed ";" do
            %a{:href => "#Dugundji66"} Dugundji 1966, XI Thm. 9.3
          = succeed ")" do
            %a{:href => "compactly+generated+topological+space#Strickland09"} Strickland 09, Prop. 1.7
          %p
          .num_prop
            %h6 Proposition
            %p
              The
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/product+topological+space"} product topological space
              of a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+compact+Hausdorff+space"} locally compact Hausdorff space
              with a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/k-space"} k-space
              is already a k-space (i.e. without need of
              = succeed ")." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/k-ification"} k-ification
          (e.g.
          = succeed "," do
            %a{:href => "#Piccinini92"} Piccinini 1992, Thm. B.6
          = succeed ")" do
            %a{:href => "compactly+generated+topological+space#Strickland09"} Strickland 2009, Prop. 2.6
          %p
          #kSpacesAreTheQuotientSpacesOfLocallyCompactHausdorffSpaces.num_prop
            %h6 Proposition
            %p
              %strong
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/k-spaces"} k-spaces
                are the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quotient+topological+space"} quotient spaces
                of
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+compact+Hausdorff+spaces"} locally compact Hausdorff spaces
              %br/
              A
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"} topological space
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/k-space"} k-space
              iff it is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quotient+topological+space"} quotient topological space
              of a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+compact+Hausdorff+space"} locally compact Hausdorff space
          This is proven in
          %a{:href => "#Dugundji66"} Dugundji 1966, XI Thm. 9.4
          (also
          = succeed ")" do
            %a{:href => "#Piccinini92"} Piccinini 92, Thm. B.4
          = succeed "." do
            %a{:href => "#EscardoLawsonSimpson04"} Escardo, Lawson &amp; Simpson 2004, Cor. 3.4 (iii)
          #kSpacesAreTheColimitsInTopOfCompactHausdorffSpaces.num_prop
            %h6 Proposition
            %p
              %strong
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/k-spaces"} k-spaces
                are the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Top#UniversalConstructions"} colimits in Top
                of
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+Hausdorff+spaces"} compact Hausdorff spaces
              %br/
              A
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"} topological space
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/k-space"} k-space
              iff it is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/colimit"} colimit
              as formed in
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Top"} Top
              (according to
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "Top#DescriptionOfLimitsAndColimitsInTop"} this Prop.
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diagram"} diagram
              of
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+Hausdorff+spaces"} compact Hausdorff spaces
          (
          %a{:href => "#EscardoLawsonSimpson04"}> Escardo, Lawson &amp; Simpson 2004, Lem. 3.2 (v)
          )
          %h3#gelfand_duality Gelfand duality
          %p
            Under
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Gelfand+duality"} Gelfand duality
            the category of compact Hausdorff topological spaces is equivalent to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/opposite+category"} opposite category
            of commutative
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/C-star+algebras"} C-star algebras
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Gelfand+duality"} Gelfand duality
            for more.
          %h3#further_properties Further properties
          %p
          .num_prop
            %h6 Proposition
            %p
              Locally compact Hausdorff spaces are
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/paracompact+space"} paracompact
              whenever they are also
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/second-countable+space"} second-countable
          %p
          #LocallyCompactHausdorffSpacesAreCompletelyRegular.num_remark
            %h6 Example
            %p
              Locally compact Hausdorff spaces are
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/completely+regular+topological+spaces"} completely regular topological spaces
          (e.g.
          = succeed ";" do
            %a{:href => "#Dugundji66"} Dugundji 1966, XI Thm. 6.4
          = succeed ")" do
            %a{:href => "#Engelking89"} Engelking 1989, Thm. 3.3.1
          .num_remark
            %h6 Remark
            %p
              Example
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#LocallyCompactHausdorffSpacesAreCompletelyRegular"}
              plays a key role in discussion of
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/slice+theorem"} slice theorems
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+proper+map"} locally proper map
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+compact+locale"} locally compact locale
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+topological+space"}> compact topological space
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/countably+compact+topological+space"} countably compact topological space
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/paracompact+topological+space"} paracompact topological space
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+compact+topological+space"} locally compact topological space
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/strongly+compact+topological+space"} strongly compact topological space
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Gelfand+duality"} Gelfand duality
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vanishing+at+infinity"} vanishing at infinity
          %h2#references References
          %p Textbook accounts:
          %ul
            %li#Dugundji66
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/James+Dugundji"}> James Dugundji
                , Section XI.6 of:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Topology
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://www.southalabama.edu/mathstat/personal_pages/carter/Dugundji.pdf"} pdf
            %li#Engelking89
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ryszard+Engelking"}> Ryszard Engelking
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em General Topology
                = succeed "," do
                  %strong 6
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://www.heldermann.de/SSPM/SSPM06/sspm06.htm"} ISBN 388538-006-4
            %li#Piccinini92
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Renzo+A.+Piccinini"}> Renzo A. Piccinini
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Lectures on Homotopy Theory
                = succeed "," do
                  %strong 171
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://www.sciencedirect.com/bookseries/north-holland-mathematics-studies/vol/171/suppl/C"} ISBN:978-0-444-89238-6
          %p Lecture notes:
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Brian+Conrad"}> Brian Conrad
              \:
              %em Paracompactness and local compactness
              \&amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "http://math.stanford.edu/~conrad/diffgeomPage/handouts/paracompact.pdf"}> pdf
              ,
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/Conrad-ParaAndLocalCompactness.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
          %p
            Further discussion in relation to
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compactly+generated+topological+spaces"} compactly generated topological spaces
          %ul
            %li#EscardoLawsonSimpson04
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mart%C3%ADn+Escard%C3%B3"}> Martín Escardó
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jimmie+Lawson"} Jimmie Lawson
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Alex+Simpson"} Alex Simpson
              = succeed "," do
                %em Comparing Cartesian closed categories of (core) compactly generated spaces
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/j.topol.2004.02.011"} doi:10.1016/j.topol.2004.02.011
